-- title:
--   Relative Cartier extension of a generic divisor on X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and $K$ the intermediate field of $L((q))/L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the coefficientwise embedding of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the pushout of the spectra of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with $k$-morphisms $i_1, i_2$ from $C_1, C_2$ to the base change $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k$ that are closed immersions, such that every point of $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and its number of points equals $n$ with $0 < n$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : A \to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ surjective with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ the structure map $A \to k$; let $bc : X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k \to X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} O$ be a morphism compatible with the first projections and with the second projections via $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Assume the kernel ideal sheaves of $bc \circ i_1$ and of $bc \circ i_2$ are invertible, in the sense that each point has an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(U)$ with the point in the basic open of $f$ and the ideal on the affine basic open of $f$ generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and that the product of these two kernels is the kernel of $bc$. Let $T'$ be a fraction field of $O$, assume the projection $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} T' \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $E$ be a relative effective Cartier divisor of degree $r$ on $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} T'$, that is, an ideal sheaf on $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} T'$ whose closed subscheme is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} T'$ with fibre rank $r$ everywhere. Then there is a relative effective Cartier divisor $\bar E$ of degree $r$ on $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ whose pullback along $\operatorname{Spec}(O \to T')$ is $E$, such that the ideal $\bar E.I$ is invertible, its pullbacks (comaps) along $bc$, along $bc \circ i_1$ and along $bc \circ i_2$ are invertible, and the closed subscheme of $\bar E.I$ pulled back along $bc$, followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, is a finite morphism.
--
--   This is the statement that the scheme-theoretic closure of an effective divisor on the generic fibre, in the base change of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ to an unramified discrete valuation ring over $A$, is again a relative effective Cartier divisor, with ideal invertible both on the total space and on the special fibre and on each of its two components, and with no vertical part. It feeds the construction of pairs of relative Cartier divisors used to compare the associated line bundles with the Poincaré bundle on the relative Picard scheme of $X_1(Mp)$.
